        "node_id": "n_4_ea19e3",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of reversing the entire stack into the result deque, use a double-ended queue (deque) to efficiently append and pop elements from both ends. This way, we can simulate the effect of appending and then reversing the sequence without fully reversing the entire deque after each operation.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "7825313280896944758",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_ea19e3_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_4e2da5ef7c",
